# Superscripts and subscripts, Position in the rule of a styled run (reference/common/text-formatting.md): page of
# 240 × 160 with margins of 20, page area of 200 × 120 from (20, 20). Size 10 with Line height 15; with the test metrics
# each character measures 5 pt, and one of a superscript or a subscript, at 70 % of the size, 3.5. They do not change
# the height of the lines. The image shows them raised and lowered.
#   units:  a superscript and a subscript in one line. y = 20.
#   plain:  "aaaa bbbb", 45 in a box of 40: two lines. y = 35.
#   raised: the same text with "bbbb" as a superscript: 20 + 5 + 4 × 3.5 = 39 fits in the 40. One line, y = 65.
#   marks:  a subscript in bold, a struck superscript, whose line goes with its letters, and an underlined one, whose
#           line stays on that of the text. y = 80.
#   notes:  a superscript next to the call of a footnote, which is at the same height. y = 95.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: es
	Title: Prueba
	Page:
		Width: 240
		Height: 160
		Margin: 20
	Styles:
		For element: Document
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Sans
				Size: 10
				Line height: 15
				Markup: markdown
		For style: sup
			Typography:
				Position: superscript
		For style: sub
			Typography:
				Position: subscript
				Color: #B3261E
		For style: narrow
			Box:
				Width: 40
	Section:
		Text: Son 10 m[2]{sup} de CO[2]{sub}.
			Id: units
		Text: aaaa bbbb
			Id: plain
			Style: narrow
		Text: aaaa [bbbb]{sup}
			Id: raised
			Style: narrow
		Text: H**[2]{sub}**O, ~~x[2]{sup}~~ y ++x[2]{sup}++.
			Id: marks
		Text: El 1[er]{sup} día[^a].
			Id: notes
		Footnote:
			Id: a
			Paragraph: Una nota.
